Package: lsastrat
Title: Stratification and Inequality Metrics for Large-Scale Assessment Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Kevin", "Schoenholzer", , "kevinschonholzer@gmail.com",
             role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9892-5869")),
      person("Swiss National Science Foundation", role = "fnd",
             comment = "Grant 205177"))
Description: Computes educational stratification and inequality quantities
    from large-scale assessment (LSA) data such as PISA, TIMSS and PIRLS as
    first-class outputs, with plausible-value pooling (Rubin's rules) and
    survey replicate-weight variance estimation (balanced repeated
    replication, including Fay's method, and jackknife). Provides the
    socio-economic achievement gradient (slope, strength and curvature),
    school-level segregation indices with a clustered bootstrap and
    finite-sample bias correction, and the Ferreira-Gignoux decomposition of
    inequality of educational opportunity. Complements general LSA packages
    (such as 'EdSurvey', 'intsvy' and 'BIFIEsurvey') by packaging
    stratification measures that those tools leave to be assembled by hand.
